Mega800:
--------

  Mega800 is a port of MiSTer's Atari800 core
      done by the MiSTer Development Team
      Original GitHub Repository: https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Atari800_MiSTer
      Significant contributors:
      * Wojciech Mostowski (woj76): maintainer; VBXE, PokeyMax integration,
        cartridge, cassette, PBI and many other extensions
      * Alexey Melnikov (sorgelig): original MiSTer port
      * claude
      * carlosbravoa

  MiSTer's Atari800 core is a port of the Atari 800XL FPGA core
      done by Mark Watson
      Original Repository: http://www.64kib.com/redmine/projects/eclairexl
      Significant contributors:
      * Mark Watson (foft): ANTIC, GTIA, POKEY, PIA, address decoder,
        PokeyMax and the overall Atari 8-bit core design

  Significant authors of modules used inside the Atari800 core:
      * Matthias Reichl (HiassofT): cartridge logic (cart_logic.vhd) and
        freezer logic (freezer_logic.vhd)
      * Peter Wendrich: 65xx CPU core (cpu_65xx.vhd, from FPGA64)
        http://www.syntiac.com/fpga64.html
      * Tomasz Piórek and Agnieszka Bartkowicz: the original VBXE hardware,
        on which the VBXE implementation by Wojciech Mostowski is based
      * Avery Lee (Altirra) and laoo: GTIA palette data; the Altirra Hardware
        Reference Manual was used for the VBXE implementation
        https://www.virtualdub.org/altirra.html
      * The cartridge type table used by the cartridge loader follows MiSTer's
        Main_MiSTer (support/atari8bit/atari800.cpp) by the MiSTer
        Development Team
        https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Main_MiSTer

Other than that and my own work, Mega800 uses:
----------------------------------------------

  * MiSTer2MEGA65 by The MiSTer2MEGA65 Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/MiSTer2MEGA65

  * QNICE Co-Processor and System-on-a-Chip for file operations and on-screen-menu by The QNICE Development Team
    https://github.com/sy2002/QNICE-FPGA

  * Various MEGA65 drivers taken from the MEGA65 VHDL source by Paul Gardner-Stephen
    https://github.com/MEGA65/mega65-core

  * VGA Timing Generator, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=15925278

  * VGA to HDMI converter IP core, done by Adam Barnes
    https://github.com/amb5l/tyto2

  * AVALON SCALER used for scaling to 720p for HDMI, done by temlib.org
    http://temlib.org/site/?page_id=10

  * HyperRAM controller, done by MJoergen
    https://mjoergen.github.io/HyperRAM/

  * Debouncer: I/O debouncing used for the joysticks, done by Scott Larson
    https://www.digikey.com/eewiki/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=4980758

  * Anikki-16x16 font, archived and provided by k80w
    https://github.com/k80w/consolefonts

  * PSF font to text file converter nafe-0.1 by Corvus Corax
    https://sourceforge.net/projects/nafe/

  * PSF font to C include file converter psftools-1.1.1 by John Elliott
    https://www.seasip.info/Unix/PSF/

